  "solution": "def solve_sudoku(board: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    b = [list(row) for row in board]\n    def is_valid(r, c, val):\n        for i in range(9):\n            if b[r][i] == val or b[i][c] == val:\n                return False\n        box_r, box_c = 3 * (r // 3), 3 * (c // 3)\n        for i in range(3):\n            for j in range(3):\n                if b[box_r + i][box_c + j] == val:\n                    return False\n        return True\n    def solve():\n        for r in range(9):\n            for c in range(9):\n                if b[r][c] == 0:\n                    for val in range(1, 10):\n                        if is_valid(r, c, val):\n                            b[r][c] = val\n                            if solve():\n                                return True\n                            b[r][c] = 0\n                    return False\n        return True\n    solve()\n    return b\n",
  "explanation": "Backtracking trial of candidate digits 1-9 for empty cells verifies row, column, and 3x3 box validity."
